  "summary": "A 300 mm specialty logic foundry fab in Dresden run by ESMC, a venture 70 percent owned by TSMC with Bosch, Infineon and NXP holding 10 percent each. Announced in August 2023 at more than 10 billion euros, it is planned for 28/22nm and 16/12nm processes and about 40,000 wafers a month, mainly for automotive and industrial chips. The European Commission approved 5 billion euros of German State aid and ground was broken in August 2024. The building was topped out in September 2026; the first process tools are due in the second half of 2027, while the original plan targeted production by the end of 2027 and the Commission cites full capacity in 2029.",
